%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1963640d94415114d8eb3f359d5b928b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Story_1_DialogueData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueSO
  locationDialogue: Floating Islands
  dialogueLines:
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: All in order on the paperwork side, deed's fully transferred, cloud-well's
      registered under your name. You're a proper landowner now, sir.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(half-listening, glancing toward the garden) Good. Good. Hey,
      actually, quick thing. '
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: Mm?
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: I've been getting... visitors. Small ones. Little dark things,
      low to the ground, keep trying to squeeze through the fence line at night.
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: (pauses, blinking) ...Visitors.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: 'Monsters. Small ones. Spawn-sized, I think, nothing I can''t handle,
      just annoying. Chewed through half a row of carrots last week. '
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: (genuinely thrown, flipping through her clipboard like the answer's
      written somewhere in it) That's, odd. Sky islands this far out don't get wildlife,
      let alone monsters. No land bridge, no roosting cover, nothing for them to
      follow up here. In eleven sales I've never once had a client report so much
      as a moth.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: So it's not normal.
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: It is not normal, no. (closes clipboard, shrugs) But, small ones,
      you said? Spawn-tier?
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: Yeah.
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: '(businesslike again, already moving on) Then frankly, sir, that''s
      well within what a retired Hero should be able to handle without troubling
      his broker. '
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: (a small, apologetic smile) Structural integrity and property lines
      are my department. Pest control is, regrettably, yours now.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (dry) Right. Comforting.
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: 'I did say it was structurally very sound. I never said pristine.
      (gathers her things) I''ll flag it in the file regardless, if it keeps up,
      or if anything bigger comes sniffing around, you send word to the guild office
      in Aldenport. Until then, enjoy the quiet, Archer. '
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: (She heads off, kicking off into the sky. As she vanishes over
      the ridge, a sky-ferry gondola descends nearby.)
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: Well. It's real. I half expected to find you sleeping in a field
      somewhere, having given up by week two.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (small grin) Give me some credit.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (looking around) I am. This is more than I expected, honestly.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: 'Where''s the idiot? Figured he''d have shown up by now to mock
      the turnips. '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (dry) Banned.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: ...From what?
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: The sky-ferry line. All of them. Apparently he got drunk on the
      Aldenport route and tried to convince the pilot the gondola "wanted to do a
      barrel roll." Guild's revoked his boarding rights indefinitely.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (laughs, shaking his head) Of course he did.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: He sends his regards. Loudly, and from a tavern, I imagine.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (sighing, gesturing toward the garden) Well, since you made it.
      Come see the place properly. Fair warning though, something's been getting
      in. Small monsters, chewing up my rows at night.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (raising an eyebrow, skeptical) Monsters. Up here.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: I know how it sounds.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: 'It sounds like something ate your vegetables and you''re blaming
      the dark instead of the wind-hares. (starts walking with him anyway) Show me. '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (They walk through the rows. As they near the center of the garden,
      the Priestess slows, her eyes fixed on something. A single sapling stands there,
      small, unremarkable at a glance, its leaves faintly catching light that doesn't
      quite match the sky.)
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (quiet, stopping completely) ...Archer. Where did you get this.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (shrugs) That one? Grew from something I picked up on the way back,
      small seed, glowed a little. Figured it'd make a decent centerpiece.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (crouching by it, studying the leaf pattern, voice tightening)
      You never once looked closely at it.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: Not really, no. Why, is it-
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (cutting in, half to herself) No wonder they've been coming. (looks
      up at him) Archer. This is a sapling of the Life Tree.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(blank for a second, then actually crouching down to look properly,
      really look, this time) ...Huh. '
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(the resemblance hits him, the bark pattern, the faint inner light
      in the leaves, unmistakable now that he''s looking) That''s, hat''s not possible,
      I found that near the- '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: Near the Tree. Yes. Some fall. Rarely, but they do.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(standing, a little pale) So the spawn aren''t random. They''re
      following it. '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: Life energy draws them. Even a fragment of it. It'd be strange
      if they weren't showing up.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(staring at the sapling now like it might do something) Okay.
      Okay, that''s,how big does this thing get, exactly? Because if I''ve got a
      Life Tree growing out of my vegetable patch- '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: '(a small laugh, standing, brushing off her robes) Relax. The Tree
      you helped free didn''t reach the sky in a season, Archer. It took a hundred
      years to grow past a man''s height. A thousand more before it looked anything
      like what you fought under. '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (glancing back at the sapling) You'll be long done with your tomatoes
      before this one so much as shades your fence.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(exhales, some tension leaving his shoulders, but not all of it)
      ...Good. That''s, good. '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (watching him a beat longer than the moment needs) ...Good.
